pySMESH: make StdMeshers_Prism_3D mesh a prism whose side face has a composite horizontal
side, when the projection of the other side fits it; else name the reason and the way out;
and forget the errors of the bottom candidates it rejected (SMESH V9_16_0).

Defect: Prism_3D cannot mesh a prism with a side face whose bottom or top side has several
EDGEs (a composite horizontal side). It builds a mesh that does not follow those EDGEs, or it
fails, and it reports the error of a FACE that it tried as the prism bottom and rejected.

Symptom: a straight prism on a regular n-gon, one bottom EDGE split at its midpoint, the top
EDGE above it whole, so the wall between them is one 5-EDGE FACE (report §3 B1). With
Regular_1D + NumberOfSegments(4), 2 on each half-EDGE, and Quadrangle_2D or MEFISTO_2D:
n = 5 fails with "Composite 'horizontal' edges are not supported", n = 6 with "Side face #27
has a composite top edge" (#27 is the top cap, not a side face), both "(algorithm Prism_3D)".
Prism_3D::Compute returns true for both. n = 4 (a box) fails with "Non-quadrilateral faces are
not opposite".

Root cause, in StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx:
* initPrism() finds no FACE that must be the bottom: removeQuasiQuads() accepts the caps and
  the 5-EDGE wall as quadrangles. It then tries the FACEs one by one (:3740-3767), with
  mySetErrorToSM = false. The true bottom (n + 1 EDGEs) is skipped by "nbFaces < 2 + nbEdges"
  (:3758-3759); the 5-EDGE wall is rejected in getWallFaces() (:1162 for n = 5, :1251-1255 for
  n = 6); the top cap is accepted. Each rejection stores its message in the algorithm
  (SMESH_Algo::error) and nothing clears it. After Compute(), whatever it returned, the solid's
  sub-mesh takes the worse of its error and the algorithm's (SMESH_subMesh.cxx:1582), and
  checkComputeError() makes it FAILED_TO_COMPUTE (:2043-2060). The several-solid path clears
  the error after each candidate (InitComputeError(), :993-996); this path does not.
* With the top cap as bottom, the 5-EDGE wall has 1 EDGE on its bottom side and 2 on its top
  side. computeWalls() meshes the top side of a wall that is not meshed yet by projecting
  side[QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE].grid->Edge(0) onto side[QUAD_TOP_SIDE].grid->Edge(0) only
  (:1925-1975): the first half-EDGE gets the 4 segments of the whole bottom EDGE, the second
  keeps its own 2. The caps then have 5 and 6 EDGEs, project2dMesh() cannot pair them, and
  projectBottomToTop() places the top nodes by the block approach (:2569-2592), because
  bottomToTopTrsf is always identity (GetLayersTransformation() is commented out, :1342-1345).
  Measured with the stale error cleared: mesh volume off the prism volume by 1.7e-5 (n = 5,
  Quadrangle_2D) to 1.3e-3 (n = 5, MEFISTO_2D) relative, 29 top cap nodes against 31 bottom
  ones, no vertical node column. A composite bottom side, which getWallFaces() accepts when
  all its EDGEs are on the bottom FACE (:1155-1163), becomes a composite top side when
  initPrism() turns the prism upside down (:3821-3825).
* On a box (n = 4) the bottom and the 5-EDGE wall are the only FACEs without 4 EDGEs and
  share the split EDGE. initPrism() takes them as the bottom and the top, because
  removeQuasiQuads() runs only for more than 2 such FACEs (:3673), and the check that they are
  opposite fails (:3803-3818).
* The search is from SMESH 9a54694a0 (2013-02-12, "Merge from V6_main 11/02/2013"); upstream
  master at 83f8bf482 has the same code.

Change, in StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx only:
* computeWalls(), a wall that is not meshed yet and has more than one EDGE on its bottom or
  top side: projectCompositeSide() projects the whole bottom side onto the whole top side, as
  computeWalls() projects a composite vertical side (:1827-1895): each node keeps its share
  of the length of the side, counted from the left side of the wall (normalized parameter,
  StdMeshers_FaceSide::Value3d() and Parameter()). A node that falls on a VERTEX splitting the
  top side within the VERTEX tolerance is that VERTEX's node. Each segment is set on the EDGE
  that holds its middle. A top side meshed already is kept if its number of segments is that
  of the bottom side. Walls with single EDGEs are meshed as before.
* getWallFaces(), first row of walls, at the point of the former refusal: a wall FACE that is
  not meshed yet and has a composite horizontal side is checked by compositeSideMismatch().
  A pre-pass over the bottom EDGEs tells whether initPrism() will turn the prism upside down
  (more bottom EDGEs than walls), so that the check takes the side that computeWalls() will
  project from. The mesh must be linear (a quadratic one is refused: the projection makes
  linear segments). The EDGEs of a composite side must join smoothly (SMESH_Algo::
  IsContinuous()), as the parts of a split EDGE do: at a corner, as where a polygon cap is a
  wall of a sweep across the solid, the caps differ in shape, and the sweep projected the
  vertical sides onto each other without their hypotheses (a regular hexagon prism with 4
  segments on each half of its split EDGE got 6 and 12 segments on EDGEs of 4).
  If the target side has several EDGEs, the projection must put a node on
  each VERTEX that splits it, and on each target EDGE the number of segments that the hypotheses
  of that EDGE give (SMESH_Algo::Evaluate(), which meshes nothing), so that no hypothesis is
  dropped. A single target EDGE takes the projection, as before. The source EDGEs are meshed
  to find their nodes, unless the total numbers of segments already differ. If the check
  fails, the FACE is not the bottom: "Side face #N has B EDGE(s) on its bottom side and T on
  its top side, and <reason>. Split the EDGE opposite the composite side at the same points,
  so that both sides have the same number of EDGEs, or give each EDGE of the composite side
  the segments that the other side projects onto it", and the search for the bottom goes on
  from the same point as before. projectCompositeSide() runs the same check again for every
  wall, and fails the compute with the reason.
* compute(): if a wall has a composite horizontal side and the prism is a translation (both
  caps planar, one row of walls, every vertical EDGE straight and the same vector),
  bottomToTopTrsf is that translation, so projectBottomToTop() places each top node above its
  bottom node. Before, the block approach placed them up to 1.5e-4 away.
* initPrism(): if exactly 2 FACEs have not 4 EDGEs and they share an EDGE, removeQuasiQuads()
  runs as for more than 2 such FACEs, and the search for the bottom skips a FACE that touches
  a shared EDGE ("FACE #N: not tried, it touches an EDGE that the 2 FACEs without 4 EDGEs
  share."). As the bottom, such a FACE makes the shared EDGEs vertical, and computeWalls()
  projects the vertical sides of a wall onto each other without their own hypotheses: on the
  box of r3d with 4 segments on every EDGE, three EDGEs got 8.
* initPrism(), search for a bottom: the reason of each FACE that is not the bottom is kept,
  "FACE #N: <its error>." or "FACE #N: not tried, it has E EDGEs and the solid F FACEs.". If a
  bottom is found, the stored error is cleared with error( COMPERR_OK ) (not
  InitComputeError(), which would also clear a cancel request). If none is found, the error is
  COMPERR_BAD_SHAPE "No FACE can be the bottom of the prism." followed by those reasons; before,
  its text was empty.

Not changed: the order of the candidates and the "2 + nbEdges" filter; a wall whose FACE is
already meshed; the projection of single EDGEs, which also ignores the hypotheses of a top
EDGE; the cap projection of a prism that is not a translation. A solid with no composite
horizontal side meshes as before, bit for bit, unless a rejected candidate's error used to fail
it, or exactly 2 FACEs without 4 EDGEs that share an EDGE used to fail it.

diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx
@@ -1102,6 +1102,384 @@
 }
 
 //================================================================================
+// pySMESH: a wall FACE whose bottom or top side has several EDGEs (a composite horizontal
+// side). computeWalls() meshes the top side of a wall that is not meshed yet by projecting
+// its bottom side onto it. For single EDGEs it projects EDGE onto EDGE. For a composite side
+// these functions project the whole bottom side onto the whole top side, as computeWalls()
+// projects a composite vertical side: a node keeps its share of the length of its side,
+// counted from the left side of the wall.
+//================================================================================
+
+namespace
+{
+  //================================================================================
+  /*!
+   * \brief Return the number of segments of an EDGE: those of its mesh, else those that
+   *        its 1D algorithm would make with its hypotheses (SMESH_Algo::Evaluate(), which
+   *        meshes nothing), or -1 if no algorithm can tell. Set isQuadratic if the
+   *        segments are quadratic.
+   */
+  //================================================================================
+
+  smIdType nbSegments( SMESH_Mesh& mesh, const TopoDS_Edge& edge, bool& isQuadratic )
+  {
+    SMESH_subMesh* sm = mesh.GetSubMesh( edge );
+    if ( sm->IsMeshComputed() )
+    {
+      SMDS_ElemIteratorPtr segments = sm->GetSubMeshDS()->GetElements();
+      if ( segments->more() && segments->next()->IsQuadratic() )
+        isQuadratic = true;
+      return sm->GetSubMeshDS()->NbElements();
+    }
+    SMESH_Algo* algo = sm->GetAlgo();
+    SMESH_Hypothesis::Hypothesis_Status status;
+    if ( !algo || !algo->CheckHypothesis( mesh, edge, status ))
+      return -1;
+    MapShapeNbElems nbElems;
+    if ( !algo->Evaluate( mesh, edge, nbElems ) || !nbElems.count( sm ))
+      return -1;
+    const std::vector< smIdType >& nb = nbElems[ sm ];
+    if ( nb.size() <= SMDSEntity_Quad_Edge )
+      return -1;
+    if ( nb[ SMDSEntity_Quad_Edge ] > 0 )
+      isQuadratic = true;
+    return nb[ SMDSEntity_Edge ] + nb[ SMDSEntity_Quad_Edge ];
+  }
+
+  //================================================================================
+  /*!
+   * \brief Mesh the EDGEs of a side that are not meshed yet. Return why one cannot be
+   *        meshed, or an empty text.
+   */
+  //================================================================================
+
+  std::string meshSideEdges( SMESH_Mesh&                   mesh,
+                             const StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr& side,
+                             const char*                   sideName )
+  {
+    for ( int i = 0; i < side->NbEdges(); ++i )
+    {
+      SMESH_subMesh* sm = mesh.GetSubMesh( side->Edge( i ));
+      if ( !sm->IsMeshComputed() )
+      {
+        sm->ComputeSubMeshStateEngine( SMESH_subMesh::COMPUTE ); // nodes on VERTEXes
+        sm->ComputeStateEngine( SMESH_subMesh::COMPUTE );        // segments on the EDGE
+      }
+      if ( !sm->IsMeshComputed() )
+        return SMESH_Comment( "EDGE #" ) << sm->GetId() << " of its " << sideName
+          << " side cannot be meshed";
+    }
+    return std::string();
+  }
+
+  //================================================================================
+  /*!
+   * \brief Return the nodes of the meshed source side of a wall, and where each falls on
+   *        the target side, as a normalized parameter of the target side. The source side
+   *        is the bottom one, or the top one if fromTop.
+   */
+  //================================================================================
+
+  bool sourceNodesOnTarget( const FaceQuadStruct&                quad,
+                            const bool                           fromTop,
+                            std::vector< const SMDS_MeshNode* >& nodes,
+                            std::vector< double >&               tgtParams )
+  {
+    StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr src = quad.side[ fromTop ? QUAD_TOP_SIDE : QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE ].grid;
+    StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr tgt = quad.side[ fromTop ? QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE : QUAD_TOP_SIDE ].grid;
+    StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr lft = quad.side[ QUAD_LEFT_SIDE ].grid;
+    src->NbPoints( /*update=*/true );
+    const UVPtStructVec& points = src->GetUVPtStruct();
+    if ( points.size() < 2 )
+      return false;
+    const bool srcFromLeft = ( src->FirstVertex().IsSame( lft->FirstVertex() ) ||
+                               src->FirstVertex().IsSame( lft->LastVertex() ));
+    const bool tgtFromLeft = ( tgt->FirstVertex().IsSame( lft->FirstVertex() ) ||
+                               tgt->FirstVertex().IsSame( lft->LastVertex() ));
+    nodes.clear();
+    tgtParams.clear();
+    for ( size_t i = 0; i < points.size(); ++i )
+    {
+      const double fromLeft = srcFromLeft ? points[ i ].normParam : 1. - points[ i ].normParam;
+      nodes.push_back( points[ i ].node );
+      tgtParams.push_back( tgtFromLeft ? fromLeft : 1. - fromLeft );
+    }
+    return true;
+  }
+
+  //================================================================================
+  /*!
+   * \brief Return the index of the EDGE of the top side that ends at the VERTEX lying at a
+   *        normalized parameter of the top side, within the VERTEX tolerance, or -1
+   */
+  //================================================================================
+
+  int splitVertexAt( const StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr& top, const double param )
+  {
+    for ( int iE = 0; iE + 1 < top->NbEdges(); ++iE )
+      if ( Abs( param - top->LastParameter( iE )) * top->Length() <=
+           BRep_Tool::Tolerance( top->LastVertex( iE )))
+        return iE;
+    return -1;
+  }
+
+  //================================================================================
+  /*!
+   * \brief Return why the source side of a wall with a composite horizontal side cannot be
+   *        projected onto its target side, or an empty text if it can. The source side is
+   *        the bottom one, or the top one if fromTop. The mesh must be linear, and the EDGEs
+   *        of a composite side must join smoothly, as the parts of a split EDGE. If the target
+   *        side has several EDGEs, the projection must put a node on each VERTEX that splits
+   *        it, and on each target EDGE the number of segments that the hypotheses of that
+   *        EDGE give, so that no hypothesis is dropped. The source EDGEs are meshed if they
+   *        are not yet, unless the numbers of segments already differ.
+   */
+  //================================================================================
+
+  std::string compositeSideMismatch( SMESH_Mesh&           mesh,
+                                     const FaceQuadStruct& quad,
+                                     const bool            fromTop )
+  {
+    StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr src = quad.side[ fromTop ? QUAD_TOP_SIDE : QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE ].grid;
+    StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr tgt = quad.side[ fromTop ? QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE : QUAD_TOP_SIDE ].grid;
+    const char*        srcName = fromTop ? "top" : "bottom";
+    const char*        tgtName = fromTop ? "bottom" : "top";
+
+    // the numbers of segments, before anything is meshed
+    std::vector< smIdType > nbTgtEdgeSeg( tgt->NbEdges() );
+    smIdType nbSrcSeg = 0, nbTgtSeg = 0;
+    bool     isKnown  = true, isQuadratic = false;
+    for ( int i = 0; i < src->NbEdges(); ++i )
+    {
+      const smIdType nb = nbSegments( mesh, src->Edge( i ), isQuadratic );
+      isKnown   = isKnown && nb >= 0;
+      nbSrcSeg += nb;
+    }
+    for ( int i = 0; i < tgt->NbEdges(); ++i )
+    {
+      nbTgtEdgeSeg[ i ] = nbSegments( mesh, tgt->Edge( i ), isQuadratic );
+      isKnown   = isKnown && nbTgtEdgeSeg[ i ] >= 0;
+      nbTgtSeg += nbTgtEdgeSeg[ i ];
+    }
+    if ( isQuadratic )
+      return "its mesh is quadratic, which a composite horizontal side does not support";
+
+    // the EDGEs of a composite side must join smoothly, as the parts of a split EDGE do: at
+    // a corner the two caps differ in shape, and the solid is no prism between them
+    const StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr sides[2] = { src, tgt };
+    const char*                  names[2] = { srcName, tgtName };
+    for ( int iS = 0; iS < 2; ++iS )
+      for ( int i = 0; i + 1 < sides[ iS ]->NbEdges(); ++i )
+        if ( !SMESH_Algo::IsContinuous( sides[ iS ]->Edge( i ), sides[ iS ]->Edge( i + 1 )))
+          return SMESH_Comment( "its " ) << names[ iS ] << " side has a corner between EDGEs #"
+            << mesh.GetMeshDS()->ShapeToIndex( sides[ iS ]->Edge( i )) << " and #"
+            << mesh.GetMeshDS()->ShapeToIndex( sides[ iS ]->Edge( i + 1 ))
+            << ", so it is not a split EDGE";
+    if ( tgt->NbEdges() < 2 )
+      return std::string(); // a single target EDGE takes the projection, as in computeWalls()
+    if ( isKnown && nbSrcSeg != nbTgtSeg )
+    {
+      SMESH_Comment edgeIDs;
+      for ( int i = 0; i < tgt->NbEdges(); ++i )
+        edgeIDs << ( i ? ", #" : "#" ) << mesh.GetMeshDS()->ShapeToIndex( tgt->Edge( i ));
+      return SMESH_Comment( "its " ) << srcName << " side has " << nbSrcSeg
+        << " segments, while the hypotheses of the EDGEs of its " << tgtName << " side ("
+        << edgeIDs << ") give " << nbTgtSeg;
+    }
+
+    const std::string notMeshed = meshSideEdges( mesh, src, srcName );
+    if ( !notMeshed.empty() )
+      return notMeshed;
+    std::vector< const SMDS_MeshNode* > nodes;
+    std::vector< double >               params;
+    if ( !sourceNodesOnTarget( quad, fromTop, nodes, params ))
+      return SMESH_Comment( "its " ) << srcName << " side has no node";
+
+    // a node on each VERTEX that splits the target side
+    for ( int iE = 0; iE + 1 < tgt->NbEdges(); ++iE )
+    {
+      const double split = tgt->LastParameter( iE );
+      double gap = 1.;
+      for ( size_t i = 0; i < params.size(); ++i )
+        gap = Min( gap, Abs( params[ i ] - split ));
+      if ( gap * tgt->Length() > BRep_Tool::Tolerance( tgt->LastVertex( iE )))
+        return SMESH_Comment( "the VERTEX that splits its " ) << tgtName << " side lies "
+          << gap * tgt->Length() << " from the nearest node of its " << srcName << " side";
+    }
+
+    // the segments of its hypotheses on each target EDGE
+    std::vector< double > sorted( params );
+    std::sort( sorted.begin(), sorted.end() );
+    std::vector< smIdType > nbProjected( tgt->NbEdges(), 0 );
+    for ( size_t i = 1; i < sorted.size(); ++i )
+      ++nbProjected[ tgt->EdgeIndex( 0.5 * ( sorted[ i - 1 ] + sorted[ i ] ))];
+    for ( int i = 0; i < tgt->NbEdges(); ++i )
+      if ( nbTgtEdgeSeg[ i ] >= 0 && nbTgtEdgeSeg[ i ] != nbProjected[ i ] )
+        return SMESH_Comment( "the hypotheses of EDGE #" )
+          << mesh.GetMeshDS()->ShapeToIndex( tgt->Edge( i )) << " of its " << tgtName
+          << " side give " << nbTgtEdgeSeg[ i ] << " segments, while the projection of its "
+          << srcName << " side puts " << nbProjected[ i ] << " on it";
+    return std::string();
+  }
+
+  //================================================================================
+  /*!
+   * \brief Mesh the top side of a wall with a composite horizontal side by projecting its
+   *        bottom side onto it as a whole. Return why it cannot, or an empty text.
+   */
+  //================================================================================
+
+  std::string projectCompositeSide( SMESH_Mesh& mesh, const FaceQuadStruct& quad )
+  {
+    SMESHDS_Mesh*        meshDS = mesh.GetMeshDS();
+    StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr  bot = quad.side[ QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE ].grid;
+    StdMeshers_FaceSidePtr  top = quad.side[ QUAD_TOP_SIDE    ].grid;
+
+    // getWallFaces() checked the walls of a bottom candidate; check every wall again, here
+    std::string why = compositeSideMismatch( mesh, quad, /*fromTop=*/false );
+    if ( why.empty() )
+      why = meshSideEdges( mesh, bot, "bottom" );
+    if ( !why.empty() )
+      return why;
+    smIdType nbBotSegments = 0;
+    for ( int i = 0; i < bot->NbEdges(); ++i )
+      nbBotSegments += mesh.GetSubMesh( bot->Edge( i ))->GetSubMeshDS()->NbElements();
+
+    int      nbTopMeshed   = 0;
+    smIdType nbTopSegments = 0;
+    for ( int i = 0; i < top->NbEdges(); ++i )
+    {
+      SMESH_subMesh* sm = mesh.GetSubMesh( top->Edge( i ));
+      sm->ComputeStateEngine( SMESH_subMesh::CHECK_COMPUTE_STATE );
+      if ( sm->IsMeshComputed() )
+      {
+        ++nbTopMeshed;
+        nbTopSegments += sm->GetSubMeshDS()->NbElements();
+      }
+    }
+    if ( nbTopMeshed == top->NbEdges() )
+    {
+      if ( nbTopSegments == nbBotSegments )
+        return std::string();
+      return SMESH_Comment( "its top side is meshed already, with " ) << nbTopSegments
+        << " segments for " << nbBotSegments << " on its bottom side";
+    }
+    if ( nbTopMeshed > 0 )
+      return "its top side is meshed already in part";
+
+    std::vector< const SMDS_MeshNode* > botNodes;
+    std::vector< double >               params;
+    if ( !sourceNodesOnTarget( quad, /*fromTop=*/false, botNodes, params ))
+      return "its bottom side has no node";
+
+    // nodes on the top VERTEXes
+    for ( int i = 0; i <= top->NbEdges(); ++i )
+    {
+      const TopoDS_Vertex v = ( i < top->NbEdges() ) ? top->FirstVertex( i ) : top->LastVertex();
+      mesh.GetSubMesh( v )->ComputeStateEngine( SMESH_subMesh::COMPUTE );
+      if ( !SMESH_Algo::VertexNode( v, meshDS ))
+        return SMESH_Comment( "VERTEX #" ) << meshDS->ShapeToIndex( v ) << " of its top side has no node";
+    }
+
+    // the projected nodes, in the order of the top side
+    std::vector< double > topParams( params );
+    std::sort( topParams.begin(), topParams.end() );
+    std::vector< const SMDS_MeshNode* > topNodes( topParams.size() );
+    topNodes.front()  = SMESH_Algo::VertexNode( top->FirstVertex(), meshDS );
+    topNodes.back()   = SMESH_Algo::VertexNode( top->LastVertex(),  meshDS );
+    topParams.front() = 0.;
+    topParams.back()  = 1.;
+    for ( size_t k = 1; k + 1 < topParams.size(); ++k )
+    {
+      const double u = topParams[ k ];
+      const int iSplit = splitVertexAt( top, u );
+      if ( iSplit >= 0 )
+      {
+        topNodes[ k ] = SMESH_Algo::VertexNode( top->LastVertex( iSplit ), meshDS );
+        continue;
+      }
+      TopoDS_Edge  edge;
+      const double t = top->Parameter( u, edge );
+      const gp_Pnt p = top->Value3d( u );
+      SMDS_MeshNode* node = meshDS->AddNode( p.X(), p.Y(), p.Z() );
+      meshDS->SetNodeOnEdge( node, edge, t );
+      topNodes[ k ] = node;
+    }
+    for ( size_t k = 1; k < topNodes.size(); ++k )
+    {
+      const int iE = top->EdgeIndex( 0.5 * ( topParams[ k - 1 ] + topParams[ k ] ));
+      SMDS_MeshEdge* segment = meshDS->AddEdge( topNodes[ k - 1 ], topNodes[ k ] );
+      meshDS->SetMeshElementOnShape( segment, top->Edge( iE ));
+    }
+    for ( int i = 0; i < top->NbEdges(); ++i )
+      mesh.GetSubMesh( top->Edge( i ))->ComputeStateEngine( SMESH_subMesh::CHECK_COMPUTE_STATE );
+    return std::string();
+  }
+
+  //================================================================================
+  /*!
+   * \brief Return true if a wall of the prism has a composite horizontal side
+   */
+  //================================================================================
+
+  bool hasCompositeHorizontalSide( const Prism_3D::TPrismTopo& prism )
+  {
+    for ( size_t iW = 0; iW < prism.myWallQuads.size(); ++iW )
+    {
+      Prism_3D::TQuadList::const_iterator quad = prism.myWallQuads[ iW ].begin();
+      for ( ; quad != prism.myWallQuads[ iW ].end(); ++quad )
+        if ( (*quad)->side[ QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE ].grid->NbEdges() > 1 ||
+             (*quad)->side[ QUAD_TOP_SIDE    ].grid->NbEdges() > 1 )
+          return true;
+    }
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  //================================================================================
+  /*!
+   * \brief Set the translation that carries the bottom FACE onto the top one, if the
+   *        prism is a translation: both FACEs planar, one row of walls, and every
+   *        vertical EDGE a straight segment of one and the same vector
+   */
+  //================================================================================
+
+  bool prismTranslation( const Prism_3D::TPrismTopo& prism,
+                         SMESH_MesherHelper&         helper,
+                         gp_Trsf&                    trsf )
+  {
+    if ( !GeomLib_IsPlanarSurface( BRep_Tool::Surface( prism.myBottom )).IsPlanar() ||
+         !GeomLib_IsPlanarSurface( BRep_Tool::Surface( prism.myTop    )).IsPlanar() )
+      return false;
+    gp_Vec vec;
+    bool   isFirst = true;
+    for ( size_t iW = 0; iW < prism.myWallQuads.size(); ++iW )
